{"id": "unknown-2026-05-15-004", "date": "2026-05-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "order_visibility", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["surpass", "loss", "decline", "plunge", "weak", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "ICE cotton falls sharply on profit booking, weak US exports", "content": "ICE cotton futures plunged sharply after a steep rally triggered heavy profit booking and long liquidation in an overbought market.\nWeak US export sales added pressure, while broader commodity-market losses deepened the decline.\nJuly 2026 cotton fell 3.31 per cent to 83.94 cents per pound, with trading volume surpassing 100,000 contracts amid heightened speculative activity.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-falls-sharply-on-profit-booking-weak-us-exports-310334-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-15-005", "date": "2026-05-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s annual WPI inflation rate 8.3% YoY in April", "content": "The annual rate of inflation based on all India wholesale price index (WPI) stood at 8.3 per cent YoY in April, provisional data show. \nThe index number and inflation rate for April of manufactured products was 151.6 and 4.62 per cent YoY respectively. \nThe YoY WPI inflation rates for textiles, apparel and leather and related products in April were 7.3 per cent, 2.2 per cent and 1.25 per cent respectively. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-annual-wpi-inflation-rate-8-3-yoy-in-april-310328-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-15-006", "date": "2026-05-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Why are garment makers betting big on the Indian state of Odisha?", "content": "Odisha is rapidly emerging as a major textile and apparel manufacturing hub, backed by plug-and-play industrial parks, strong policy support and large investments from companies including Page Industries and Epic Group. \nWith over ₹7,000 crore investments and thousands of jobs in the pipeline, the state aims to become the textile capital of eastern India by 2030. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/why-are-garment-makers-betting-big-on-the-indian-state-of-odisha--310327-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-15-007", "date": "2026-05-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India's FY26 GDP growth estimated at 7.5%: SBI", "content": "Despite global headwinds, India has maintained strong growth momentum, an SBI newsletter said. \nRural consumption remains strong and urban consumption shows a consistent uptick since the last festive season. \nIt expects Q4 FY26 real GDP growth of closer to 7.2 per cent and nowcasts FY27 GDP growth rate of 6.6 per cent. \nFY26 GDP growth is likely to be at 7.5 per cent. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-fy26-gdp-growth-estimated-at-7-5-sbi--310314-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
